<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>

<section xml:id="section-extrema" >
<title>Absolute and Relative Extrema</title>

<introduction>
	<p>One of the uses of derivatives is to identify traits of functions such as highest and lowest points. These are optimizations in many applications (i.e., find the lowest cost or maximum profit).</p>
</introduction>

<subsection xml:id="subsection-use-derivative-absolute-extrema" >
	<title>Absolute Extrema</title>

	<p>First, we will think about traits of highest and lowest points on specified sections of curves (functions over a limited domain).</p>

	<p>An <term>absolute maximum</term> is the highest point of a function/curve on a specified interval. An <term>absolute minimum</term> is the lowest point of a function/curve on a specified interval. Collectively maxima and minima are known as <term>extrema</term>.</p>

	<definition xml:id="definition-absolute-maximum">
		<title>Absolute Maximum</title>
		<statement><p>A value <m>c \in [a,b]</m> is an <term>absolute maximum</term> of a function <m>f</m> over the interval <m>[a,b]</m> if and only if <m>f(c) \ge f(x)</m> for all <m>x \in [a,b]</m>.</p></statement>
	</definition>

	<definition xml:id="definition-absolute-minimum">
		<title>Absolute Minimum</title>
		<statement><p>A value <m>c \in [a,b]</m> is an <term>absolute minimum</term> of a function <m>f</m> over the interval <m>[a,b]</m> if and only if <m>f(c) \le f(x)</m> for all <m>x \in [a,b]</m>.</p></statement>
	</definition>

	<activity xml:id="activity-absolute-extrema">
		<title>Identifying Absolute Extrema</title>
		<introduction><p>The goal of this activity is to determine where we should look for absolute extrema.</p></introduction>
		<task><p>Identify the absolute maxima and absolute minima for each function in <xref ref="figure-absolute-extrema-activity" /> in the intervals specified. The intervals are specified by the green, dashed vertical lines.</p></task>
		<task><p>Using these examples determine where on a function absolute extrema can be found.</p></task>
		<task><p>Construct another absolute extrema practice problem for another group to solve.</p></task>
	</activity>

<figure xml:id="figure-absolute-extrema-activity">
