</figure>

</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="subsection-relative-extrema">
	<title>Identifying Relative Extrema</title>

	<p>A <term>relative maximum</term> is a location on a curve where all points near it are lower. A <term>relative minimum</term> is a location on a curve where all points near it are higher.</p>

	<definition xml:id="definition-relative-maximum">
		<title>Relative Maximum</title>
		<statement><p>A value <m>c</m> in the domain of a function <m>f</m> is a <term>relative maximum</term> of <m>f</m> if and only if there exists some interval <m>(a,b)</m> in the domain containing <m>c</m> such that <m>f(c) \ge f(x)</m> for all <m>x \in (a,b)</m>.</p></statement>
	</definition>

	<definition xml:id="definition-relative-minimum">
		<title>Relative Minimum</title>
		<statement><p>A value <m>c</m> in the domain of a function <m>f</m> is a <term>relative minimum</term> of <m>f</m> if and only if there exists some interval <m>(a,b)</m> in the domain containing <m>c</m> such that <m>f(c) \le f(x)</m> for all <m>x \in (a,b)</m>.</p></statement>
	</definition>

	<activity xml:id="activity-relative-extrema">
		<title>Identifying Relative Extrema</title>
		<introduction><p>The goal of this activity is to determine where we should look for relative extrema.</p></introduction>
		<task><p>Identify the relative maxima and relative minima for each function in <xref ref="figure-relative-extrema-activity" />. </p></task>
		<task><p>Draw the tangent line to the curve at each relative extreme point. What is the slope of these tangents? How is slope of a tangent calculated?</p></task>
		<task><p>Using these examples develop a method for finding relative extrema.</p></task>
	</activity>

<figure xml:id="figure-relative-extrema-activity">
	<caption>Finding Relative Extrema.</caption>

	<sbsgroup>
	<sidebyside widths="35%, 35%">
		<image source="images/relextrema1" />
		<image source="images/relextrema2" />
	</sidebyside>
	<sidebyside widths="35%, 35%">
		<image source="images/relextrema3" />
		<image source="images/relextrema4" />
	</sidebyside>
	</sbsgroup>
</figure>

	<activity xml:id="activity-possible-extrema">
		<title>Conditions for Extrema</title>
		<introduction><p>The goal of this activity is to discover properties of curves that have specific types of extrema.</p></introduction>
		<task><p>Draw one curve for each of the following sets of conditions.</p>
		<p><ol>
			<li>One relative maximum, two relative minima</li>
			<li>One relative minimum, two relative maxima</li>
			<li>One relative minimum, no relative maxima</li>
			<li>Two relative minima, no relative maxima</li>
			<li>One absolute maximum, one absolute minimum</li>
			<li>One absolute maximum, two absolute minima</li>
			<li>One absolute maximum, two relative maxima</li>
			<li>No absolute maximum</li>
		</ol></p>
		</task>
		<task><p>Conjecture conditions for when absolute extrema must exist.</p></task>
	</activity>

</subsection>

</section>
